# Dialogue for the placeholder adventure. See ../../../events/FORMAT.md, "String tables".
language en

tidewater.arrival.ferry = The ferry bumps against the pilings of Tidewater Landing.
tidewater.arrival.ropes = Mind the ropes. The guide waits by the noticeboard.

tidewater.guide.bell = You came about the bell? It rings every night at Bell Cove, east past the reeds.
tidewater.guide.ask = Will you look into it?
tidewater.guide.apprentices = Then take my apprentices. One knows a spark or two, the other knows bandages.
tidewater.guide.later = Come back when you change your mind.
tidewater.guide.name_ask = Before you go: what should the harbor call you?
tidewater.guide.name_reply = Tell the ferry I am staying a while.
tidewater.guide.quiet = Quiet nights again. The whole harbor owes you a supper.
tidewater.guide.topics = Ask about...
tidewater.guide.topic_bell = The bell
tidewater.guide.topic_reeds = The reeds
tidewater.guide.about_bell = Something made of brass guards it. Rest at the inn before you go.
tidewater.guide.about_reeds = Small pests, mostly. Walk around them if you can.

tidewater.dockhand.request = A crate of my supplies washed into the reeds last storm. Nobody will wade out for it.
tidewater.dockhand.ask = Keep an eye out for it?
tidewater.dockhand.accepted = Bless you. It sits on a dry patch, north side of the path.
tidewater.dockhand.declined = Fair enough. The reeds bite.
tidewater.dockhand.reminder = North side of the path, on the dry patch. You cannot miss it.
tidewater.dockhand.found = You found it? Keep the coin, it was yours the moment you got your boots wet. Take these too.
tidewater.dockhand.thanks_again = Every ferry that docks, I tell them about you.

tidewater.hold.gnawing = Something is gnawing at a crate in the ferry hold. It turns to face you.
tidewater.hold.cleared = The hold falls quiet. A tonic rolls out from behind the crate.
tidewater.hold.empty = Only tooth marks are left on the crate.

tidewater.chart.read = A tide chart is nailed to the post by the water stairs. Someone has circled tonight's low water in red.
tidewater.chart.mystic = Low water at dusk. Leave now and we cross the reeds with dry boots.
tidewater.chart.medic = That circle is a thumbprint. Low water is at midnight, and midnight is when the bell rings.
tidewater.chart.warning = Mind that post! Something lives under it!
tidewater.chart.crab = A crab as wide as a cart wheel climbs out from under the post, claws raised.
tidewater.chart.crab_gone = The crab scuttles back under the stairs. A tonic is wedged between the planks.
tidewater.chart.crab_won = The crab clacks once, satisfied, and slides back under the post.

tidewater.board.read = Notes cover the board by the inn. A fresh one in the guide's hand asks for two more pairs of hands for the cove.
tidewater.board.engineer = That note is ours. If the bell has gears, I will find out which one sticks.
tidewater.board.scout = And I have mapped these reeds twice over. Wait for us at the gate next time.

reed.scout.joins = Heading for the cove? I have mapped these reeds twice over. I am coming along.
reed.peddler.greeting = Psst. Best prices this side of the marsh, and the only prices.
reed.peddler.farewell = Mind the wisps. They hum before they bite.
reed.skimmer.moored = A reed skimmer bobs at its mooring, its boiler still warm.
reed.skimmer.ask = Take the skimmer out across the marsh?
reed.skimmer.won = The wisps scatter. This old hull can take a beating.
reed.skimmer.declined = The skimmer knocks gently against its post.
reed.skimmer.idle = The skimmer rests at its mooring, steam curling from the vent.
reed.lookout.climb = An old reed-cutters' lookout leans over the path. The ladder groans all the way up to its platform.
reed.lookout.view = Tidewater's lamps to the west, the skimmer's mooring to the east, and nothing but reeds and wind between.
reed.lookout.peddler = Wave all you like up there! My prices look even better from down here.
reed.lookout.skimmer = The skimmer's boiler is lit. Somebody has been out on the water since dusk.
reed.lookout.gust = The whole platform is swaying. Grab the rail!
reed.lookout.climber = Something with far too many legs is coming up the ladder behind the party.
reed.lookout.won = It drops back into the reeds with a splash and does not come up again.
reed.lookout.lost = The party scrambles down the far side of the lookout, bruised but whole.
reed.lookout.down = From the path the lookout is only a crooked shape against the sky.

cove.bell.frame = A cracked bell hangs from a driftwood frame. Something stirs beneath it.
cove.bell.warden = That is no bell keeper. That is a {name:bell_warden}!
cove.bell.won = It is only gears now. The bell can rest.
cove.bell.lost = The party wakes at the inn, sore and humbled.
cove.quiet.tide = For the first time in a week, the tide is the only sound in the cove.
cove.campfire.embers = Someone left a fire banked under the cliff. The embers still glow.
cove.campfire.ask = Rest by the fire? It costs a little driftwood.
cove.campfire.rested = The warmth draws the ache out of everyone.
cove.campfire.declined = The embers settle back into the ash.
cove.campfire.journal = The firelight is good enough to write by.

saltgrass.kilnwright.story = The old kiln down the east stair fired every pot in this market. Then the sea came in and drowned it.
saltgrass.kilnwright.ask = Its heart-stone still holds an ember. Will you carry it up to me?
saltgrass.kilnwright.accepted = Take the east gate and go down past the galleries. The heart-stone sits in the firing pit, lowest floor.
saltgrass.kilnwright.declined = Then I will keep my hands warm on cold tea a little longer.
saltgrass.kilnwright.reminder = The firing pit, lowest floor. Mind the steam on the stairs.
saltgrass.kilnwright.ember = You brought the ember. Look at it, still breathing. Take these, and come back when the first new pots are fired.
saltgrass.kilnwright.thanks = The new kiln draws well. Every pot in the market carries your thumbprint now, in a way.
saltgrass.lamplighter.greeting = Evening already? I light this square before anyone else is awake.
saltgrass.lamplighter.topics = Ask about...
saltgrass.lamplighter.topic_kiln = The kiln
saltgrass.lamplighter.topic_canal = The canal
saltgrass.lamplighter.about_kiln = Steam still comes up the east stair on still nights. Things nest in warm places.
saltgrass.lamplighter.about_canal = Three bridges, and a different stubborn family rebuilt each one.
saltgrass.ferrywoman.cold = No boats run on the canal while the kiln is cold. There is nothing to carry.
saltgrass.ferrywoman.warm = The kilnwright is firing again. I will have crates to row by morning.

kiln.upper.arrival = Warm fog rolls along the galleries. Shelves of half-fired pots stand in the shallow water.
kiln.lower.draft = A hot draft breathes up from somewhere ahead. The firing pit is close.
kiln.lower.heart_unknown = A round stone sits in the pit, faintly warm. It does not seem to want anything from you.
kiln.lower.heart_glow = The heart-stone pulses at your touch. A single ember lifts free and settles in a clay cup.
kiln.lower.heart_dark = The heart-stone is cool now. Its ember has gone up to the market.

flats.mooring.note = The reed skimmer is tied to the post, with a tag in the owner's hand: "Yours for the bell. Mind the shallows."
flats.mooring.given = The skimmer rocks as if it knows you. Climb aboard from the shore beside it.
flats.mooring.aboard = The empty post creaks against the hull.
flats.mooring.recall = Pull the skimmer back to its mooring?
flats.mooring.recalled = A rope, a heave, and the skimmer is home at the post.
flats.mooring.left = The skimmer stays where you left it.
flats.beacon.cold = A cold beacon stands on the rock. You strike its flint and the oil catches.
flats.beacon.answer = Far to the west a second light answers. By morning the ferry will run to the isles.
flats.beacon.lit = The beacon burns steadily. The ferry to the isles is running.

# Text the game shows itself, not a script: speaker names, the quest log, the encyclopedia and party talk.
choice.yes = Yes
choice.no = No

speaker.dockhand = Dockhand
speaker.ferrywoman = Canal Ferrywoman
speaker.guide = Harbor Guide
speaker.kilnwright = Kilnwright
speaker.lamplighter = Lamplighter
speaker.peddler = Reed Peddler

objective.meet_guide = Find the harbor guide by the noticeboard.
objective.reach_cove = Follow the reed path east to Bell Cove and find what rings the bell.
objective.report_back = Tell the harbor guide the bell is quiet.
objective.done = Enjoy the quiet nights at Tidewater Landing.

job.lost_cache = The dockhand's lost crate

codex.tidewater.title = Tidewater Landing
codex.tidewater.text = A ferry town built on pilings. Its noticeboard is the only post office for three bays.
codex.bell_warden.title = {name:bell_warden}
codex.bell_warden.text = A clockwork keeper wound to guard the cove bell. Nobody remembers who wound it.

talk.reeds.1 = Every step out here squelches. I am counting them.
talk.reeds.2 = Count the bites instead. I am the one who has to dress them.
talk.chapter_one.1 = A bell that rings by itself. I would like to meet whoever pulls the rope.
talk.after_bell.1 = Supper at the harbor, then. I hear the guide promised.
talk.market.1 = A town that smells of salt and clay. I could get used to this.
talk.market.2 = Get used to it after we rest. My feet are done.
talk.kiln.1 = Watch the water. Some of those pots are not pots.
talk.kiln.2 = It is warmer down here than it has any right to be.
